# Documentation sync (homecloud-docs)

**Mandatory:** when you add or change **user-facing** CLI behavior (commands, flags, URIs, auth), update the docs site in the **same task** — never defer.

**Live site:** https://docs.web.holab.abrdns.com  
**Docs repo:** sibling `homecloud-docs/` (MkDocs; auto-deploys on push to `main`)

## This repo → docs

| Change | Update docs under |
|--------|-------------------|
| Commands, flags, URIs, auth | `docs/en/cli/` (+ `docs/he/cli/` for key pages) |
| Release / version tag | Row in `docs/en/cli/releases.md` (+ HE) |

## Conventions

- **SO** not "storage" — URIs: `so://bucket/key`
- CLI examples: show PowerShell **and** bash when quoting/JSON differs
- Code blocks, commands, JSON: always **LTR**

## Workflow

1. Implement here
2. Edit `homecloud-docs/docs/en/cli/...` (and HE for key pages)
3. Run `mkdocs build --strict` in `homecloud-docs/`
4. Ship docs with the code when the user asks to push
5. Mention the docs update in your summary

## Do not

- Ship CLI changes without updating docs
- Say "docs can be updated later"
- Use `s3://` in new docs (accept in CLI for compat only; docs use `so://`)
